# Analysis-pane rules

Use the shared primitives. Do not rebuild card / header / list / loading shells per panel.

## Primitives (under `frontend/src/components/analysis/`)

- `AnalysisSection` — `<section>` + `SectionHeader` + spacing. Use for every titled block in a panel.
- `AnalysisCard` — card shell. Variants: `default`, `accent`, `compact`. Use for selection results, QA answers, assumption rows, derivation steps.
- `AnalysisAccordionRow` — collapsible row.
- `AnalysisTabs` — config-driven tab strip. Tabs are data: `{ id, label, feature?, pinned?, badge?, icon? }`.
- `OverflowMenu` — base-ui Popover wrapper (replaces hand-rolled portal menus).
- `RichContent` — renders `ContentBlock[]`.
- `StreamingMarkdown` — wraps `RichContent` with the streaming cursor + badge.
- `useSelectionThread` — single source of truth for selection messages, status, history. Replaces ad-hoc streaming logic.
- `useStreamingObject` — generic AI SDK `useObject` wrapper with abort + idempotency + zustand persistence.

## Visual language (carry from recent commits — no new tokens)

- Card bg: `bg-card/30 dark:bg-card/22`. Chrome bg: `bg-muted/[0.08]`.
- Borders: `border-border/50` standard; `border-border/40` chrome.
- Spacing: `space-y-8` between sections; `space-y-3` inside; `space-y-2` for list items.
- Typography: `font-display` for headings; `tracking-[-0.02em]` for h3; body `text-[var(--text-sm)]`.
- Motion: only `motion-safe:duration-150` color transitions and the existing streaming-cursor blink. **No new animations.**
- Shadows: only `var(--shadow-xs)` and `var(--shadow-sm)`.
- Focus: `focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring`.

## Hard rules

- No new colors, no new shadow tokens, no new motion durations. Audit yourself: any new className must already exist somewhere in the codebase, or carry a one-line comment justifying it.
- Streaming UX (cursor, "streaming…" badge, pulse footer) lives in **one** component (`StreamingMarkdown`). Never reimplement.
- Tab strip is data-driven via `AnalysisTabs`. Do not hand-write `<TabsTrigger>` arrays in panel hosts.
- Position cycle and font scale live inside `OverflowMenu`. Do not portal a bespoke menu.
- Lazy-mount tabs on first visit, then keep mounted. The `AnalysisTabs` primitive owns this; panel hosts don't.

## Component LOC budget (refactor target)

- `BottomPanel.tsx` ≤ 200 LOC.
- `SelectionResultPanel.tsx` ≤ 250 LOC.
- `SummaryPanel.tsx` ≤ 160 LOC.
- New panels: keep below the equivalent budgets.
